{:id "0053-lab-flick"
 ;; Split on 2026-11-18: the board's build alone cost $7.70, so this order is
 ;; the pure half of the flick and 0058 is the page.
 :title "Lab flick, the pure half: one exam as data (a pair that is easy to tell apart, its timeline, the choice)"
 :lupa/deps #{"0051-lab-board" "0052-lab-dress"}
 :lupa/area :lab
 :lupa/risk :medium
 :goal "docs/product/score.md, 'How people and agents drive it', and the
        H5 result in docs/product/lab-notebook.md. People will not tune
        parameters, but they can tell which of two performances they
        prefer. On request, the lab reads the current line back twice, as
        A (your style now) and B (one step along one axis), you flick
        toward the one you like, and your style point moves (lab.learn).
        The H5 simulation says this only works when the two are easy to
        tell apart, so a pair that would look the same is never offered."
 :scope ["src/halfahead/lab/flick.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/flick_test.cljc"
         "src/halfahead/lab/learn.cljc" "test/halfahead/lab/learn_test.cljc"]
 :design "halfahead.lab.learn gains (existing functions unchanged):
          (skip state) -> the state asking about the next axis, with
            nothing else changed (no flick counted).
          halfahead.lab.flick (.cljc, pure): one exam, as data.
          (distinct? plan-a plan-b) -> whether two reading plans
            (lab.reading/plan) would look or sound different: the marks
            performing or their gestures differ, or the dress differs, or
            the motion parameters of their points differ by at least 10%
            in tempo or amplitude or 0.2 in overshoot.
          (offer learn-state text pace) -> {:state s :axis k :a plan :b
            plan :point-a p :point-b p}, or nil when the text is not a
            message or no axis gives a distinct pair: take (learn/pair s);
            if its two plans are not distinct, (learn/skip s) and try the
            next axis, at most four times.
          (phases offer) -> the exam's timeline in ms from its start:
            [{:phase :a :at 0 :ms da} {:phase :gap ..400} {:phase :b ..db}
            {:phase :choose ..}], da and db each the reading's length
            (stops and cues) plus 300 ms.
          (phase-at phases t) -> the phase in force at t.
          (decide offer choice) -> the learn state after choosing :a or :b
            (learn/choose on the offer's state).
          Tests: learn/skip; distinct? for plans that differ in each way
          and for two that do not; offer skipping an axis that shows
          nothing on a bare line and returning nil for an empty one;
          phases and phase-at; decide moves the point exactly as
          learn/choose does. Property: for any text and learn state, offer
          is nil or its two plans are distinct and its points differ on
          exactly one axis."
 :acceptance
 ["flick and learn tests as in the design, on both hosts; `bb test` stays
   green"]
 :non-goals
 ["Never start an exam unprompted; no telemetry; nothing leaves the device"
  "No change to learn's existing functions, reading, pace, marks, score,
   gestures, synth, dress, the board's pads, the renderer or the director;
   do not edit the schema"
  "No page, no lab.main, no browser check: order 0058"
  "Do not run `bb e2e`, `bb play` or `bb lab:e2e`"]
 :context ["docs/product/score.md" "src/halfahead/lab/learn.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/reading.cljc" "src/halfahead/lab/style.cljc"
           "src/halfahead/lab/dress.cljc" "DESIGN.md"]
 :budget-usd 8.0}
